  "description": "Now £1,200, was £1,700. Save £500 in the Summer Sale while stocks last.\nThe Kinesis G2 has been winning over the UK cycling press since it launched, earning a Cycling Weekly Editor's Choice award, a Bike Perfect Recommended badge and a Cyclist magazine Great Value award. All of those verdicts came in at the full retail price of £1,700. This summer it's now £500 less.\nThe G2 bike is built around a simple but powerful idea: one bike that handles everything British riding throws at it. More capable than a disc road bike. More comfortable than a cyclocross racer. More versatile than a dedicated gravel bike. Whether it's fast lanes, muddy bridleways, a big day out or the daily commute, the G2 is at home on all of them.\nBuilt around a double-butted 6061 aluminium frame and a full UD carbon fork, the G2 comes with SRAM Apex 1x hydraulic disc brakes, tubeless-ready Schwalbe G-One Allround tyres and rack and mudguard mounts as standard. 45mm tyre clearance gives you the freedom to spec it for whatever terrain you have in mind.\nThe G2 is built to take it wherever you want to go – two of our ambassador riders even picked the G2 for ultra-endurance adventure races across Europe, on both the Transcontinental Ride and the challenging VIA Race - proving that this is a bike that can pretty much handle anything.\nKinesis has been designing bikes in the UK for over 25 years. The G2 is the result of everything that experience has taught us about what makes a great all-roads bike for British riders.\nKinesis G2 video review - by Guy Kesteven",
